Record a bootstage mark before every post-relocation initcall, off by default.

bootstage only marks board_init_f, board_init_r, main_loop and the bootm
stages, so on this board the whole post-relocation init is a single 302 ms
step between two records - five times what the same U-Boot and SoC take on
a trimmed tree, with nothing in the configuration to explain it.

With CONFIG_BASEOS_INITCALL_TIMING the initcall sequence in board_r.c records
the arch counter before each call, so one boot gives the split from
/proc/device-tree/bootstage/record@*/name + mark. Diagnostic builds only: it
costs one timer read per initcall and pushes the record list past its
default 50, so raise CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE_RECORD_COUNT with it.

The decoration is applied in board_r.c, not in INITCALL() itself. board_f.c
uses the same macro 68 times before relocation, where the timebase and the
driver model are not up yet; marking there hangs the board before it can
report anything.

BOOTSTAGE_ID_ALLOC rather than a fixed id: bootstage_add_record() keeps only
the first record for a given id, so a fixed id would collapse the whole
sequence into one entry.

diff --git a/boot/Kconfig b/boot/Kconfig
--- a/boot/Kconfig
+++ b/boot/Kconfig
@@ -1297,6 +1297,18 @@
 		};
 
 	  Code in the Linux kernel can find this in /proc/devicetree.
+
+config BASEOS_INITCALL_TIMING
+	bool "Record a bootstage mark before every initcall"
+	depends on BOOTSTAGE
+	help
+	  Record the timer before each entry in the post-relocation initcall
+	  sequence, named after the function. Bootstage otherwise only marks
+	  the start of board_init_r and of main_loop, which hides the whole
+	  sequence behind one number.
+
+	  Diagnostic builds only: this costs a timer read per initcall and
+	  needs CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE_RECORD_COUNT raised to fit the sequence.
 
 config BOOTSTAGE_STASH
 	bool "Stash the boot timing information in memory before booting OS"
diff --git a/common/board_r.c b/common/board_r.c
--- a/common/board_r.c
+++ b/common/board_r.c
@@ -598,6 +598,29 @@
  * TODO: perhaps reset the watchdog in the initcall function after each call?
  */
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_BASEOS_INITCALL_TIMING
+/*
+ * Record the arch counter before each call in this sequence, named after the
+ * function. Done here rather than in INITCALL() itself: board_f.c uses the
+ * same macro and runs before the timebase and driver model are up, where a
+ * mark hangs the board before it can report anything.
+ *
+ * BOOTSTAGE_ID_ALLOC gives each record a fresh id, because
+ * bootstage_add_record() keeps only the first record per id and a fixed one
+ * would collapse the whole sequence into a single entry.
+ */
+#undef INITCALL
+#define INITCALL(_call) \
+	do { \
+		bootstage_mark_name(BOOTSTAGE_ID_ALLOC, #_call); \
+		if (_call()) { \
+			printf("%s(): initcall %s() failed\n", __func__, \
+			       #_call); \
+			hang(); \
+		} \
+	} while (0)
+#endif
+
 static void initcall_run_r(void)
 {
 	/*
